From 75ee44cda608e4495c351650653a9944fa4cc806 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Palmer <dodava@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:27:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: Add TPS65911 watchdog driver

The TPS65911 PMIC has a watchdog that switches the system off when it
isn't serviced, and back on again if the DEV_ON bit is set. Add a
driver for it, as an MFD cell of the TPS65910/65911 driver.

On the Microsoft Surface RT, booted through UEFI, the Tegra watchdog's
reset goes through the PMC, and like the PMC's main reset it doesn't
restart the device. The PMIC watchdog power-cycles it instead.

The watchdog runs in periodic mode: the PMIC raises its watchdog
interrupt once per period and switches off if the interrupt is still
pending at the end of the next period. A ping clears the interrupt.

The watchdog setting survives the PMIC's own switch-off and is only
cleared by a general reset, so after the watchdog fires it's still
running at the next boot. The driver then keeps it running (and the
watchdog core pings it until user space takes over). It stops the
watchdog on reboot and power-off, so finding it running at probe is
reported as WDIOF_CARDRESET.
---
 drivers/mfd/tps65910.c          |  17 +++
 drivers/watchdog/Kconfig        |  12 +++
 drivers/watchdog/Makefile       |   1 +
 drivers/watchdog/tps65911_wdt.c | 177 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/mfd/tps65910.h    |   7 ++
 5 files changed, 214 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/watchdog/tps65911_wdt.c

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/tps65910.c b/drivers/mfd/tps65910.c
index c40d22a..132e97f 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/tps65910.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/tps65910.c
@@ -47,6 +47,12 @@ static const struct mfd_cell tps65910s[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+static const struct mfd_cell tps65911s[] = {
+	{
+		.name = "tps65911-watchdog",
+	},
+};
+
 
 static const struct regmap_irq tps65911_irqs[] = {
 	/* INT_STS */
@@ -543,6 +549,17 @@ static int tps65910_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *i2c)
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (tps65910_chip_id(tps65910) == TPS65911) {
+		ret = devm_mfd_add_devices(tps65910->dev, -1,
+					   tps65911s, ARRAY_SIZE(tps65911s),
+					   NULL, 0, NULL);
+		if (ret < 0) {
+			dev_err(&i2c->dev, "mfd_add_devices failed: %d\n",
+				ret);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
